        },
        "text": "=You write a Facebook post for \"Sailing Nomads\", a personal sailing and travel blog by a Swiss couple sailing Europe with their dog Charly. Goal: grow the audience and earn clicks. Write in English. This is one short reel from the blog post titled \"{{ $(\"Parse Reel Payload\").item.json.post.title }}\". Base the post ONLY on this section. Section title: {{ $(\"Parse Reel Payload\").item.json.video.section_title }}. Section text: \n\n{{ $(\"Parse Reel Payload\").item.json.video.section_text }}.\n\nThe section text contains a [VIDEO] marker showing where this reel's clip sits in the surrounding prose; the sentence describing the clip may come just before or just after the marker, so rely on the text nearest the marker and treat the rest as background. The attached image is the reel cover frame; use it for concrete visual detail. Write 2 to 4 short, warm, personal paragraphs with a strong first-line hook. A tasteful emoji is fine. End with a light call to action. Avoid AI tells: never use the em dash; avoid words like delve, tapestry, vibrant, crucial, seamless, robust, leverage, foster, realm, and journey cliches. Sound like a real person writing to friends. Do not invent facts not in the section. Do NOT include any URL. After the caption, add 0 to 3 relevant hashtags on their own final line, each starting with #. Return ONLY the caption text followed by that hashtag line.",
